WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.610
Near Tuktoyaktuk, in Arctic Canada, a
hill rises out of the flat tundra: Ibyuk.

2
00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.110
It is 49 metres high
and 300 metres across:

3
00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.410
Canada's tallest hill of its kind.

4
00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:17.710
And it is one of about
1,350 in the region.

5
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.210
Its core is solid ice.

6
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:21.590
How did it get there?

7
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.210
Did a glacier dump it?

8
00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.640
Did wind pile up snow and soil?

9
00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:28.210
In this mission, you'll define permafrost,

10
00:00:28.260 --> 00:00:32.230
and find out why estimates
of its area disagree.

11
00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:35.690
Then you'll read the patterns that
ice wedges carve into the ground,

12
00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:38.950
and the signs of a thawing Arctic.

13
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.710
Your mission: explain how a 49-metre
hill with a core of solid ice formed near

14
00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:45.760
Tuktoyaktuk.
